s($,"bZ7","bpq",()=>{var q="Comparison",p="Trend",o="Part-to-whole",n="One non-negative total split into a few categories.",m="Distribution",l="Relationship",k="Contribution and decomposition",j="Geographic",i="Target and performance",h="Advanced analytical charts"
return A.b([A.dc(q,"Bar chart","Horizontal bars compare values across discrete categories.","Use when category names are long or ranking matters.","Category plus numeric measure.","Which categories are larger or smaller?","Easy to rank and compare; long labels fit.","Too many categories create a long chart; use a consistent scale.","Compare revenue across branches."),A.dc(q,"Column chart","Vertical bars compare values across categories or ordered periods.","Use for a modest number of categories or periods.","Category or period plus numeric measure.","How do values differ across groups or periods?","Familiar and effective for clear differences.","Long labels are awkward; bar baselines should normally start at zero.","Compare monthly sales across four products."),A.dc(q,"Grouped bar chart","Places bars side by side to compare series within each category.","Use when direct comparison between a small number of series matters.","Category, series and numeric measure.","How does each series compare within a category?","Preserves individual series values.","Crowds with many series or categories.","Compare actual and budget revenue by branch."),A.dc(q,"Stacked bar chart","Stacks component values into a total for each category.","Use when both total size and composition matter.","Category, component and additive numeric measure.","What makes up each category total?","Shows totals and composition together.","Only the baseline segment is easy to compare precisely.","Show expense categories within each branch total."),A.dc(q,"Lollipop chart","Shows a point value connected to a baseline by a thin line.","Use for a clean ranked comparison.","Category and numeric measure.","Which categories rank highest or lowest?","Less visual ink than thick bars.","Less familiar; small differences may be hard to perceive.","Rank branches by satisfaction."),A.dc(p,"Line chart","Connects ordered observations to show change over time or sequence.","Use for time series with consistent intervals.","Ordered time and numeric series.","How is the measure changing over time?","Shows direction and turning points.","Irregular intervals can mislead; too many lines clutter.","Track weekly revenue for a year."),A.dc(p,"Area chart","Fills area beneath a line to emphasize magnitude over an ordered axis.","Use when total volume matters as well as trend.","Ordered time and numeric measure.","How does volume evolve over time?","Emphasizes scale and continuity.","Filled areas can obscure overlap and exaggerate visual weight.","Show daily website visits."),A.dc(p,"Stacked area chart","Stacks time-series areas to show components of a changing total.","Use for a few non-negative additive series.","Time plus additive component measures.","How does total and composition change over time?","Shows total movement and contribution.","Middle layers lack a common baseline.","Show product-family sales mix by month."),A.dc(p,"Sparkline","A compact, axis-light trend line beside a metric.","Use for quick context in tables and KPI summaries.","Short ordered numeric series.","What has the recent direction looked like?","Compact for scanning many metrics.","Not suited to detailed comparison or precise reading.","Show recent orders beside each branch KPI."),A.dc(p,"Moving average chart","Plots a rolling average to smooth short-term variation.","Use when noise hides the trend; state window length.","Ordered numeric observations and rolling window.","What is the smoothed direction?","Reduces short-term noise.","Lags turning points and may hide brief changes.","Compare daily demand with its 7-day average."),A.dc(o,"Pie chart","Slices represent parts of one whole.","Use only for a few mutually exclusive categories summing to a meaningful total.",n,"What share does each category represent?","Recognizable for simple composition.","Avoid many categories, negative values or unrelated totals; angles are hard to compare.","Share of revenue from three product lines."),A.dc(o,"Donut chart","A pie-like composition chart with a central hole.","Use for a few mutually exclusive shares, often with a total in the centre.",n,"How is the total divided?","Can display a central total.","Slice comparisons remain imprecise.","Customer mix across three plans."),A.dc(o,"Treemap","Nested rectangles sized by values show hierarchical composition.","Use for many categories or hierarchy when space is limited.","Hierarchy and non-negative size measure.","Which groups occupy the largest share?","Compact hierarchy and relative size.","Small rectangles and similar values are hard to compare.","Expense allocation by department and type."),A.dc(o,"100% stacked bar chart","Normalizes each stacked bar to 100% to compare composition.","Use when proportions matter more than absolute totals.","Category, component and non-negative additive values.","How does composition differ between groups?","Makes percentage mix comparable.","Hides group size; middle segments are difficult to compare.","Payment-method mix across branches."),A.dc(m,"Histogram","Groups continuous observations into bins and displays frequencies.","Use to inspect shape, spread, skew and multiple peaks.","One numeric variable and binning rule.","How are numerical observations distributed?","Reveals shape and concentration.","Appearance depends on bin width and boundaries.","Inspect invoice amounts."),A.dc(m,"Box plot","Summarizes median, quartiles, interquartile range and possible outliers.","Use to compare spread and outliers across groups.","Numeric variable and optional group.","Which groups vary more and where are unusual values?","Compact group comparison.","Hides multimodality and most individual observations.","Compare resolution times by branch."),A.dc(m,"Violin plot","Combines a density shape with summary information.","Use to compare distribution shapes when sample sizes support density estimates.","Numeric observations and optional group.","Do groups have different shapes or multiple modes?","Shows more shape detail than a box plot.","Density can be unstable for small samples.","Compare waiting-time distributions by location."),A.dc(m,"Density plot","A smoothed estimate of a continuous variable distribution.","Use to compare shapes without histogram bin edges.","Continuous numeric variable, optionally grouped.","Where are values concentrated?","Smoothly reveals shape and multiple peaks.","Bandwidth changes appearance; height is not a raw count.","Compare order values across channels."),A.dc(m,"Frequency polygon","Connects frequencies at bin midpoints.","Use to compare frequency shapes for multiple groups.","Binned numeric observations and frequencies.","How do group frequency patterns differ?","Overlays distributions clearly.","Depends on bin choice and may be less familiar.","Compare training-score distributions by team."),A.dc(l,"Scatter plot","Plots paired numeric observations on two axes.","Use to explore association, clusters, non-linearity and outliers.","Two numeric variables per observation.","Do two measures move together or form patterns?","Shows individual points and non-linear patterns.","Overplotting hides dense regions; correlation is not causation.","Explore discount rate versus order margin."),A.dc(l,"Bubble chart","Uses position for two variables and bubble size for a third.","Use when a third quantitative measure adds context.","Two numeric axes plus non-negative size measure.","How do three numeric measures vary together?","Adds a third dimension.","Area comparisons are imprecise; bubbles overlap.","Compare branch sales, margin and customer count."),A.dc(l,"Heatmap","Colour intensity encodes values in a matrix or grid.","Use to scan patterns across two categorical or ordered dimensions.","Two dimensions and numeric measure.","Where are high and low values concentrated?","Highlights clusters and hotspots.","Colour scale and perception affect interpretation.","Ticket volume by hour and weekday."),A.dc(l,"Correlation matrix","A table or heatmap of pairwise correlation coefficients.","Use for exploratory screening of pairwise associations.","Multiple numeric variables and specified correlation method.","Which variables have stronger positive or negative associations?","Summarizes many pairs compactly.","Not causal; can hide confounding and non-linear links.","Review sales, discount, traffic and margin."),A.dc(k,"Waterfall chart","Sequential positive and negative contributions bridge a start value to an end value.","Use to explain the bridge between two totals.","Starting total, signed changes and ending total.","Which factors explain the change?","Makes positive and negative contributions explicit.","Requires correct running-total logic and reconciliation.","Bridge budget profit to actual profit."),A.dc(k,"Pareto chart","Ranks categories by contribution with a cumulative-percentage line.","Use to identify categories contributing most to a total problem or outcome.","Categories and non-negative contribution values.","Which categories account for most of the total?","Prioritizes improvement opportunities.","The 80/20 pattern is not guaranteed; define denominator.","Rank defect types by total defects."),A.dc(k,"Decomposition chart","Breaks an aggregate metric into components or dimensions.","Use to drill from a headline metric into component contributions.","A measure with additive components or defined decomposition.","Which segments account for the overall result?","Connects headline outcomes to segments.","Some decompositions are model-dependent, not causal.","Break revenue change into volume, price and mix."),A.dc("Process","Funnel chart","Shows counts or values across sequential process stages.","Use when each stage represents a comparable cohort.","Ordered stages and stage counts or conversion rates.","At which stage are the largest drop-offs?","Makes stage loss visible.","Stage populations must be comparable.","Leads through qualified, proposal and sale."),A.dc("Process","Sankey diagram","Weighted flows between nodes show how quantities move.","Use when flow paths and transfers matter.","Source node, target node and non-negative flow weight.","Where do resources or transactions flow?","Reveals dominant paths and diversions.","Many nodes and crossing links become unreadable.","Customer movement between channels and plans."),A.dc(j,"Choropleth map","Colours geographic regions according to a normalized or comparable rate.","Use for rates or ratios, not raw counts when populations differ.","Geographic boundary and comparable rate.","Where are rates higher or lower?","Shows regional spatial patterns.","Large regions dominate visually; denominator matters.","Complaints per 1,000 customers by district."),A.dc(j,"Symbol map","Places sized or styled markers at geographic locations.","Use for point events, sites or counts.","Latitude/longitude or geocoded locations and measure.","Where are sites or events concentrated?","Preserves location and can show magnitude.","Overlapping symbols can mislead.","Branch locations sized by customer visits."),A.dc(j,"Geographic heatmap","Shows spatial concentration using aggregated intensity.","Use for dense point events and hotspot exploration.","Geocoded observations and aggregation or density rule.","Where do events cluster spatially?","Highlights hotspots.","Smoothing radius changes appearance; not a regional rate.","Delivery-request hotspots in a city."),A.dc(i,"KPI card","Displays a key metric with context such as target, period or change.","Use for headline metrics that need quick scanning.","Defined metric, value, unit, period and comparator.","What is the current value and is it on track?","Fast to read on dashboards.","Without context or comparator the number has little meaning.","Monthly recurring revenue with target and YoY change."),A.dc(i,"Gauge chart","Shows a value on a bounded arc or dial.","Use sparingly for one bounded progress measure with meaningful thresholds.","Actual, minimum, maximum and optional threshold bands.","Where does the value sit in a defined range?","Familiar status communication.","Consumes space; imprecise for comparisons.","Capacity utilization against safe limits."),A.dc(i,"Bullet chart","Compares a primary measure with a target and qualitative performance ranges.","Use for compact, precise actual-versus-target reporting.","Actual, target and defined qualitative ranges.","How far is actual performance from target?","Compact and more precise than a gauge.","Threshold bands need meaningful definitions.","Branch revenue actual versus budget."),A.dc(i,"Actual vs target chart","Displays achieved values alongside planned or target values.","Use to track goal attainment across categories or periods.","Actual and target on a common scale.","Where are targets met, exceeded or missed?","Makes performance gaps explicit.","Targets need consistent scope and definition.","Monthly hiring actuals versus plan."),A.dc(h,"Control chart","Plots a process measure over time with a centre line and statistically derived control limits.","Use to distinguish common-cause variation from special-cause signals.","Time-ordered process data and suitable control-chart model.","Is the process statistically stable?","Supports process monitoring.","Control limits are not specification limits or business targets.","Monitor daily packaging defects per batch."),A.dc(h,"Run chart","Plots observations in time order, often with a median reference line.","Use as a first step to identify shifts, trends and runs.","Time-ordered observations.","Is the process showing a non-random pattern?","Simple and assumption-light.","No control limits or full stability assessment.","Track daily customer wait time."),A.dc(h,"Radar chart","Plots multiple measures on radial axes.","Use for few profiles and consistently scaled dimensions.","Comparable normalized measures per entity.","How does a profile vary across dimensions?","Shows a multi-metric profile.","Area and angle mislead; clutter increases quickly.","Compare branches across service, cost and quality."),A.dc(h,"Gantt chart","Shows tasks as bars across a time axis with start, finish and optional dependencies.","Use for project schedules and overlapping workstreams.","Task, start, end and optional dependency.","When does each activity occur and what depends on what?","Communicates schedule and overlap.","Large plans become dense; critical path needs explicit encoding.","Plan discovery, build and rollout activities."),A.dc(h,"Calendar heatmap","Uses a calendar grid with colour intensity for daily values.","Use to reveal weekday, seasonal and event patterns.","Date and daily measure.","Which dates or recurring periods stand out?","Connects daily variation with calendar context.","Colour scale and missing days need clear treatment.","Daily order volume across a year."),A.dc(h,"Candlestick chart","Shows open, high, low and close values for each interval.","Use for market prices or data with meaningful OHLC structure.","Time interval and open, high, low, close.","What was the price range and direction within each interval?","Encodes intraperiod range and closing direction.","Requires valid OHLC data; can be noisy at unsuitable scales.","Review daily share-price movement.")],t.Ya)})
s($,"c_2","bCs",()=>{var q="Descriptive analytics",p="Numeric observations",o="Diagnostic analytics",n="Predictive analytics",m="Prescriptive analytics"
return A.b([A.fo(q,"Mean","Arithmetic average of observations.","Use when the mean is representative and outliers are understood.","Average order value was \u20b91,850.",p,"What is the average level?"),A.fo(q,"Median","Middle value in sorted observations.","Use for skewed values or when extremes distort the mean.","Median resolution time was 2.4 hours.","Ordered numeric observations","What is the central observation?"),A.fo(q,"Mode","Most frequently occurring value or category.","Use to identify the most common response.","The most common support issue was password reset.","Categorical or discrete values","What occurs most often?"),A.fo(q,"Minimum and maximum","Smallest and largest observed values.","Use to establish endpoints and inspect extremes.","Monthly sales ranged from \u20b94.2 lakh to \u20b912.8 lakh.",p,"What are the observed endpoints?"),A.fo(q,"Range","Maximum minus minimum.","Use for quick total spread alongside robust measures.","Delivery time ranged from 1 to 12 days.",p,"How wide is the observed span?"),A.fo(q,"Standard deviation","Square root of variance, expressed in original units.","Use when mean-based spread is appropriate.","Demand averaged 500 units with a 42-unit standard deviation.",p,"How dispersed are values around the mean?"),A.fo(q,"Frequency","Number of times a value, event or category occurs.","Use to count events and build frequency tables.","There were 126 delivery delays this month.","Event or category records","How often does this occur?"),A.fo(q,"Distribution analysis","Examines shape, centre, spread and tails.","Use before choosing summary statistics or thresholds.","Invoice amounts were right-skewed, so median was reported with mean.","Numeric variable","What pattern do observations follow?"),A.fo(o,"Variance analysis","Compares actual performance with budget, forecast, target or prior period.","Use to quantify a gap and prioritize investigation.","Actual expense exceeded budget by \u20b92.4 lakh.","Actual and comparable reference","Where and by how much did actual differ?"),A.fo(o,"Root cause analysis","Structured investigation to identify underlying mechanisms behind a problem.","Define the problem, validate evidence and test candidate causes.","A 5-Why review traced late dispatches to stock-reconciliation delays.","Process evidence and segmented measures","Which underlying factors explain the failure?"),A.fo(o,"Correlation analysis","Measures strength and direction of association between variables.","Use for exploration and hypothesis generation, not proof of cause.","Discount rate and gross margin showed a negative association.","Paired observations","Which variables tend to move together?"),A.fo(o,"Contribution analysis","Quantifies how segments or components contribute to an aggregate result.","Use to prioritize the largest contributors to change or cost.","Three product lines accounted for 72% of incremental revenue.","Total and additive components","Which segments explain most of the total?"),A.fo(o,"Segmentation","Splits a population into meaningful groups with shared characteristics.","Use to reveal differences hidden by overall averages.","Retention was compared by tenure and acquisition channel.","Records and grouping attributes","Which groups behave differently?"),A.fo(o,"Drill-down analysis","Moves from aggregate results into progressively detailed dimensions.","Preserve the same metric definition at each level.","A regional sales gap was traced to one branch and product category.","Consistent measure and hierarchical dimensions","Where exactly is the pattern concentrated?"),A.fo(n,"Linear regression","Estimates a linear relationship between an outcome and predictors.","Check linearity, residuals, assumptions and validation.","Estimate sales associated with ad spend while controlling for seasonality.","Outcome, predictors and historical observations","How does the outcome vary with predictors?"),A.fo(n,"Time-series forecasting","Uses time-ordered history, trend and seasonality to estimate future values.","Use regular or model-supported intervals and sufficient history.","Forecast weekly demand for inventory planning.","Time-stamped observations","What values are likely in future periods?"),A.fo(n,"Moving averages","Smooths a series by averaging observations in a rolling window.","Use for short-term smoothing or a simple baseline forecast.","A 4-week moving average reduced weekly demand noise.","Ordered numeric series and window","What is the recent smoothed level?"),A.fo(n,"Trend analysis","Identifies long-run direction and structural movement.","Check seasonality, structural breaks and definition changes.","Three years of data showed gradual improvement in repeat purchase rate.","Ordered observations","What broad direction is emerging?"),A.fo(n,"Classification","Predicts a discrete class or category, often with a probability score.","Use when outcome classes are defined and labelled consistently.","Classify support tickets by urgency for human review.","Labelled examples and features","Which category is this case likely to belong to?"),A.fo(n,"Forecast intervals","Intervals express uncertainty around a future observation or forecast.","Use with a point estimate; disclose coverage and horizon.","Demand forecast was 8,500 units, with an 80% prediction interval of 7,900\u20139,200.","Forecast model and error assumptions","How uncertain is the future value?"),A.fo(m,"Optimization","Finds the best feasible decision under an objective and constraints.","Use when trade-offs and constraints can be expressed quantitatively.","Optimize delivery routes within vehicle capacity limits.","Decision variables, objective and constraints","Which feasible choice best meets the objective?"),A.fo(m,"Scenario planning","Compares coherent alternative futures and their implications.","Use when key drivers are uncertain and contingency plans matter.","Compare base, downside and upside demand before staffing decisions.","Assumptions, scenarios and outcomes","What happens under plausible conditions?"),A.fo(m,"Sensitivity analysis","Tests how results change when assumptions or inputs vary.","Use to identify assumptions that most influence a decision.","Test profit when material costs rise by 2%, 5% or 8%.","Model inputs and plausible ranges","Which assumptions have the greatest effect?"),A.fo(m,"Decision analysis","Structures choices, outcomes, probabilities and consequences.","Use for uncertain choices and explicit trade-offs.","Compare supplier contracts using expected cost and delivery risk.","Alternatives, outcomes, likelihoods and criteria","Which option has the best expected outcome?"),A.fo(m,"Resource allocation","Assigns limited people, time, budget or capacity across competing needs.","Use when demand competes for scarce resources.","Allocate service staff using forecast demand and skill requirements.","Capacity, demand, priorities and constraints","Where should limited resources be assigned?")],t.Ya)})
